Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Poppr 1.1.2 released

Here is a link to all the details <https://github.com/grunwaldlab/poppr/releases/tag/v.1.1.2>

This release incorporates all of the functionalities that have been added in the development version including:

bootstrapping of any genetic distance
handling polyploid data
easier manipulation of hierarchical population structures with the genclone object
an easy method for AMOVA
Again, you can find out all of what has been added in the release notes <https://github.com/grunwaldlab/poppr/releases/tag/v.1.1.2>

It is also important to point out that the vignette has been greatly shortened so as to only include data manipulation. For examples of analyses, you can visit a primer that was written by myself, Sydney E. Everhart, and Niklaus J. Grünwald here <http://grunwaldlab.github.io/Population_Genetics_in_R>.

All of this can be installed from CRAN using the function

install.packages("poppr")

If poppr has not been built for your system yet, you can use:

install.packages("poppr", type = "source")

if you have a C compiler (on Mac that would be bundled with the free XCode app).

Once you have poppr installed, you can type
package?poppr
To see what's new.

Cheers,
Zhian

